{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/45","id":4686660691,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABF1jEUw","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/45","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/45.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/45.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/45","number":45,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"9900007: reviewed synchronous coupling obstruction; broader target unresolved","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Scoped partial result; broad question unresolved\nA one-sided binary process has shifted laws converging weakly to the stationary mixture of constant paths, but under every coupling with that limit its coordinate mismatch probability tends to 1/2. Thus Thorisson Problem 3.3's illustrative synchronous metric-convergence proposal fails even in probability.\n\nThe broader request for some other two-process coupling characterization remains unresolved. This is not a counterexample to the distinct setwise-convergence problem 9900005. One substantive approach was used.\n\n## Independent review\nSeparate adversarial review: PASS for the scoped synchronous counterexample, with unchanged proof SHA-256 `7123c345d3ecdf4fecb8941596687da54c44e169831eb23177ea485fa8386722`.\n- 885 author assertions reproduced exactly\n- 3,044 independent exact assertions pass\n- Arbitrary-coupling, full-path conditioning, metric and dependent finite-offset arguments independently audited\n- Review code, receipts and required frozen proof snapshot included\n\nThe review is independent AI review, not formal verification, external peer review or a novelty certificate.\n\n## Source boundary\nThe complete relevant original section was recovered as indexed primary PDF text, but direct retrieval of the complete original PDF failed. Published-preview and Asmussen-source limitations are retained. Historical priority is unestablished. The ordinary Skorohod/Dudley family-of-copies theorem is not misrepresented as a single-path coupling.\n","created_at":"2026-09-30T06:19:27Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T06:21:13Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a55aa47c22d81c28e859d922c6ce78c3a7cd01d2","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/45/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/45/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/45/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/d9b4acf5d070d1f04ffac86a4f08916a5629ff16","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:dot/math-9900007","ref":"dot/math-9900007","sha":"d9b4acf5d070d1f04ffac86a4f08916a5629ff16","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4",